<Solution>
    <!--
        catlog.lib / catlog.sim and both test projects are the game-free surface: they build and
        test on a machine with no KSA install.

        mod/catlog/ (MeowSci.Catlog, the actual game mod) was added in WP8, resolving deviation A2.
        It compiles against the KSA reference assemblies, which Directory.Build.props locates in
        this order: the KSA_DLL_DIR env var, then a `ksa-game-assemblies` checkout cloned as a
        SIBLING of this repo, then the per-OS game install. A machine with none of those cannot
        build this project — and therefore cannot build the solution — which is the deliberate
        trade recorded in docs/DECISIONS.md: the alternative (leaving it out) means the one project
        that couples to the game is the one project CI never compiles.
    -->
    <Project Path="catlog.lib/catlog.lib.csproj" />
    <Project Path="catlog/catlog.csproj" />
    <Project Path="catlog.sim/catlog.sim.csproj" />
    <!--
        catlog.loadgen is the high-volume harness (many randomised players against a live
        catlogd). It sits beside catlog.sim rather than inside it because the sim is a
        deterministic acceptance tool whose six scenarios are asserted to exact leaderboard
        values, and mixing a randomised mode into it would put that at risk. The dependency
        runs one way only: loadgen references the sim for its vehicle/step modelling and its
        read-API client, and nothing in the sim knows loadgen exists.
    -->
    <Project Path="catlog.loadgen/catlog.loadgen.csproj" />
    <Project Path="catlog.lib.tests/catlog.lib.tests.csproj" />
    <Project Path="catlog.integration.tests/catlog.integration.tests.csproj" />
</Solution>
